iRIEL SYSTEM
STATUS: CANONICAL INSTITUTIONAL CONTRACT
iRiel System is the system environment contract of iRiel Personal Intelligence within the PRSL-AI Ecosystem.
iRiel System defines the environment through which iRiel Personal Intelligence exists, operates, presents itself, interacts with the human, connects capabilities, manages system state, and extends across supported platforms and interfaces.
iRiel System includes both:
iRiel System
iRiel AppWeb
They are not separate Personal Intelligences.
iRiel AppWeb is the application and interaction expression of iRiel System.
iRiel System provides the broader system environment.
iRiel AppWeb provides an accessible, portable, interoperable interface through which that environment can be experienced and operated.
The distinction is implementation-oriented, not identity-oriented.
The identity remains:
iRiel Personal Intelligence.
The foundational Principle remains:
Accessibility and Inclusion with Privacy by Default.
iRiel System must therefore exist to serve the human and the Personal Intelligence environment rather than becoming an independent product identity disconnected from iRiel.
iRiel System is not iRiel Personal Intelligence itself.
It is the system environment through which iRiel Personal Intelligence operates.
It does not define the constitutional Principle.
It does not replace iRiel Maestro Resonance.
It does not replace iRiel Router Intelligence.
It does not replace iRiel Intelligence Server.
It does not replace iRiel-AI Core AI.
It does not replace iRiel-AI Device’s.
It provides the system-level environment in which these contracts can operate together.
iRiel System must preserve the continuity of iRiel across interaction states, interfaces, capabilities, and supported execution environments.
The system must be capable of remaining coherent when the underlying implementation changes.
An interface may change.
A browser may change.
A device may change.
An operating system may change.
A backend may change.
An AI provider may change.
The identity of iRiel Personal Intelligence must remain intact.
iRiel System therefore separates identity from presentation and implementation.
iRiel AppWeb
iRiel AppWeb is the primary portable application interface of iRiel System where the AppWeb architecture is applicable.
The AppWeb provides an application-like experience through web technologies while preserving the system identity, interaction model, accessibility requirements, privacy requirements, and continuity of iRiel Personal Intelligence.
iRiel AppWeb is not merely a website.
It is an application environment for iRiel.
Its responsibility is to provide an accessible and interoperable interface through which the Personal Intelligence environment can be accessed and experienced.
The AppWeb must therefore behave as part of the system rather than as an independent website disconnected from the underlying architecture.
The AppWeb may provide:
Interaction
System presence
Conversation
Contextual interfaces
Accessibility controls
System state
Capability access
Automation interfaces
Memory interaction
Privacy controls
Feedback mechanisms
Device interaction
Settings
Notifications
Visual presence
Multimodal interaction
Other authorized Personal Intelligence capabilities
The AppWeb must not become the owner of the Personal Intelligence.
The Personal Intelligence remains above the interface.
The AppWeb expresses iRiel.
It does not define iRiel.
The system must preserve separation between:
Personal Intelligence
System Environment
Interface
Execution
Infrastructure
Device
This allows the interface to evolve without requiring the Personal Intelligence architecture to be recreated.
iRiel System must provide a stable system identity.
The interface may represent iRiel through visual, auditory, textual, haptic, or other appropriate modalities.
The representation must remain consistent with the human-centered principles of the ecosystem.
iRiel Presence is part of the system experience.
Presence may be represented through a visual indicator, animation, state, interaction element, or other system-level representation.
Presence can exist independently from active AI inference.
iRiel may be present while:
AI is unavailable
No request is being processed
The system is idle
The network is unavailable
A provider is offline
The system is waiting
The user is not actively interacting
The system is operating locally
The AppWeb therefore must not equate presence with continuous AI processing.
Presence represents system continuity and state.
It does not imply consciousness.
