The system must use device capabilities according to permission, context, accessibility requirements, privacy constraints, and human intent.
Device capability does not imply authorization.
The presence of a sensor does not imply that it should be used.
The presence of a microphone does not imply continuous recording.
The presence of a camera does not imply continuous vision processing.
The system must respect explicit and implicit platform-level permission boundaries.
iRiel System must be privacy-aware.
The AppWeb must minimize unnecessary exposure of Personal Intelligence information.
