The system must not treat the browser or AppWeb as an unrestricted container for personal information.
Sensitive information should be handled according to the applicable privacy contract and system policies.
Where local processing is appropriate, local execution should be preferred.
Where remote processing is required, the system should communicate through authorized and controlled pathways.
iRiel System must support privacy-preserving degradation.
If a capability requires remote processing and remote processing is unavailable or unauthorized, the system should not silently expose information merely to preserve functionality.
Privacy constraints have priority over unnecessary convenience.
iRiel System must support authentication and authorization mechanisms appropriate to the environment.
Authentication establishes access.
Authorization establishes what may be accessed or executed.
The system must not treat successful authentication as unrestricted authorization.
Different capabilities may require different authorization levels.
